>> title: Cobb Salad
>> category: Salads
>> tags: chicken, bacon, egg, avocado, blue cheese
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: cobb salad, cobb, the cobb, chopped cobb salad, brown derby salad, california cobb
>> pairs-with: blue-cheese-dressing, basic-vinaigrette
>> servings: 4
>> time: 55 min
>> slack: forgiving — every row is cooked and cooled separately, so the only clock is the avocado, and that one starts when you cut it

>> step: render 10 min
Render @thick-cut bacon{6%slices} in a cold #skillet{} over medium heat for ~render{10%min}, then drain it and keep the fat for something else.

>> step: boil 8 min, chill hard
Boil @eggs{3%large} for ~boil{8%min} in water at a bare bubble, then ~chill{5%min} them in ice water.

>> step: poach 15 min
Poach @chicken breasts{1%lb}(450 g) with @kosher salt{1%tsp} and @bay leaf{1} in a #saucepan{} of barely trembling water for ~poach{15%min}, then let them cool in the liquid.

>> step: peel and halve
Peel and halve @&(~2)chilled eggs{}, then cut each half in three along its length.

>> step: dice to one size
Dice @&(~2)poached chicken{}, @&(~4)rendered bacon{}, @avocado{1%large}(pitted), @ripe tomatoes{2%medium}(seeded) and @blue cheese{3%oz}(85 g) into pieces of the same half-inch, keeping each one in its own pile.

>> step: lay in rows
Lay @&(~1)diced rows{} and @&(~2)cut eggs{} in stripes across @romaine{1%head}(shredded fine) and finish with @chives{2%Tbs}(sliced thin) and @blue cheese dressing{1/2%cup}(120 mL) poured down the middle.

The stripes are the recipe. A cobb is never tossed in the kitchen — you look at seven things then mix them yourself.
